        <h3>Map Features</h3>
        <fieldset>
            <legend>Adding New Maps</legend>
            Each map must be uploaded as a png image. Once the image is uploaded, it will appear on the 'View Maps' page, 
            where already existing benches can then be plotted onto the map. Each image will standardize to a maximum width 
            of 850px while maintaining the original proportions. If the image does not fill the entire width of the page, it 
            is likely too small and should be replaced by a larger image.
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
            <legend>Plotting Benches</legend>
            Benches must have already been added to the database using the 'Add Bench' page before they can be plotted on
            a map. Each map will have it's own form underneath it through which you can plot pre-existing benches. First, select
            from the dropdown menu which bench you would like to plot. Then, insert the X and Y coordinates to place the bench on
            the map. X and Y coordinates are taken as pixels, with (0, 0) being the top left and each map being 850px wide for 
            reference. If the placement of the bench is off after mapping, you can remap the same bench with new coordinates and it 
            will updated. Benches will appear as a circle containing the bench's corresponding number within its park. If the bench 
            is unavailable for purchase, it will show with a red X through it. When benches are purchased and updated in the app, 
            the maps will automatically reflect this.
        </fieldset>

